I managed to work around the issue on llama.cpp master by changing the template to apply the `trim` filter to reasoning_content so:

```diff
--- step-3.7-flash.jinja
+++ step-3.7-flash.jinja
@@ -48,6 +48,8 @@
                 {%- set reasoning_content = '' %}
             {%- endif %}
         {%- endif %}
+        {%- set reasoning_content = reasoning_content|trim %}
+        {%- set content = content|trim %}
         {%- if loop.index0 > ns.last_query_index %}
             {{- '<|im_start|>' + message.role + '\n<think>\n' + reasoning_content + '\n</think>\n' + content }}
         {%- else %}
@@ -87,4 +89,3 @@
 {%- if add_generation_prompt %}
     {{- '<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n' }}
 {%- endif %}

```

This is essentially what I did on #24985 (but only in the reasoning content there), which I still believe should be done unconditionally because it might be actually causing bugs in other models. One lesson that this investigation has taught me is that even a single extra surrounding linefeed around  might cause the model to drift and degrade performance, and the template is fully capable to add surrounding space/lines if it is necessary to make the prompt match the model's training.

