Please try this tiny patch :

```
diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/simd-mappings.h b/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/simd-mappings.h
index fca5119e1..4179605d5 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/simd-mappings.h
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/simd-mappings.h
@@ -29,13 +29,14 @@ extern "C" {
 // FP16 to FP32 conversion

 // 16-bit float
-// on Arm, we use __fp16
+// on Arm, we use __fp16, which requires the IEEE fp16 format: implied on AArch64, selected by
+//     -mfp16-format=ieee on 32-bit Arm, where the compiler may otherwise reject the type
 // on x86, we use uint16_t
 //
 // for old CUDA compilers (<= 11), we use uint16_t: ref https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/10616
 // for     MUSA compilers        , we use uint16_t: ref https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/11843
 //
-#if defined(__ARM_NEON) && !(defined(__CUDACC__) && __CUDACC_VER_MAJOR__ <= 11) && !defined(__MUSACC__)
+#if defined(__ARM_NEON) && defined(__ARM_FP16_FORMAT_IEEE) && !(defined(__CUDACC__) && __CUDACC_VER_MAJOR__ <= 11) && !defined(__MUSACC__)
     #define GGML_CPU_COMPUTE_FP16_TO_FP32(x) neon_compute_fp16_to_fp32(x)
     #define GGML_CPU_COMPUTE_FP32_TO_FP16(x) neon_compute_fp32_to_fp16(x)

```

__ARM_NEON only signals NEON availability, while __fp16 additionally requires the IEEE half format, which is implied on AArch64 but must be selected with -mfp16-format=ieee on 32 bit Arm, so gating the block on __ARM_FP16_FORMAT_IEEE restores the generic lookup path for that one configuration and leaves every toolchain that already provides the type on the exact same code.

I've tested the patch with my cross setup and it seems to work, however I feel I need to test it with a native compile before this can be merged. This will need a few days, native compile is slow. 

Maybe you can draft a pullrequest? I can comment there once testing is completed, or ping you here.

