At the moment this issue seems to be from a behavior change deployed in recent Windows which changes how the Shared GPU memory size is calculated, and the Vulkan drivers have not accommodated such change.

Previously iGPU memory size was always 50% of system RAM, but now it is calculated as the following:

- TotalSystemMemoryAvailableForGraphics = MIN((TotalSystemMemory * 80%), MAX((TotalSystemMemory - 16GB), (TotalSystemMemory * 50%))

For 64GB RAM this will be 48GB (75% cut) which matches the value for the current `heapBudget`. I believe `VkMemoryHeap::size` is still being calculated as a 50% cut (or the setting specified by the user as "[Shared GPU/NPU memory override](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/support/articles/000101789/graphics.html)" on Intel for LNL+)
I believe we need to implement a workaround in ggml.

https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-hardware/drivers/display/calculating-graphics-memory

We can add a sanity check, but shouldn't this be a very simple fix on the driver side? It means your driver is currently not following the spec: `The heapBudget value must be less than or equal to VkMemoryHeap::size for each heap.` ([Source](https://docs.vulkan.org/refpages/latest/refpages/source/VkPhysicalDeviceMemoryBudgetPropertiesEXT.html#_description))

Yes, I believe the driver will eventually be fixed, but this will take time for deployment and will only be enabled on new drivers. People with older drivers and [legacy support platforms](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/support/articles/000101986/graphics.html) will not get the fix so it'd be great if we can have a workaround in ggml.

